From 29ed1458328aad7240a89844f3bb85cdfa2e5fcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhu1025960209-web <255052750+zhu1025960209-web@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:42:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] RT: add opt-in AMD RDNA 2+ hardware BVH4 intersection
 (VICTORY_HW_BVH=1)

Adapt MeMako's upstream hardware BVH4 ray-node intersection design
(Marvisak/VIctory#3294, 8c919e6) onto the flat 1-level VRAM-side
memory.rs directory, gated behind opt-in VICTORY_HW_BVH=1 (off by default):

- Enable IAmdExtD3DShaderIntrinsics::IntersectBvhNode (opcode 0x22) via
  amdxc64.dll on verified AMD DXR-capable hardware adapters (CheckSupport
  0x19 on RDNA 2/3, 0x0D fallback on RDNA 4), with silent software
  fallback on non-AMD GPUs, WARP, or unsupported drivers.
- Add SLOT_MEMORY_VAS (t252, space1) parallel 16 MiB VRAM-side 64-bit
  host GPU VA page table in memory.rs (allocated only when active) and
  SLOT_AMD_EXT (u0, space2147420894) magic UAV bindings across shader
  emission, pipeline root-signature construction, and draw/dispatch.
- Lower image_bvh*_intersect_ray through IntersectBvhNode with per-lane
  software fallback (and SLOT_FAULTS recording) for unmapped, out-of-
  directory, partial, unaligned, or page-straddling nodes.
- Mix VICTORY_HW_BVH=1 and the active opcode into shader_cache's build
  key only when active, leaving the default software cache 100% intact.
- Add DXIL validation, live GPU correctness (bvh64-sorted, bvh32-sorted,
  bvh32-unsorted), throughput microbenchmark, and page_va unit tests.

AI-assisted (Antigravity).
